WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.434 --> 00:00:03.260
(applause)

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:06.150
We must have been the two
tallest guys in late night.

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:06.983
Yeah.

00:00:06.983 --> 00:00:08.306
Let me ask you something,

00:00:08.306 --> 00:00:10.180
because first of all that suit

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.180
you did not get that off
the rack, I'm guessing.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.013
No, no, no.

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:14.945
You have someone who makes these for you.

00:00:14.945 --> 00:00:15.848
Yes.

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:16.681
You are six feet

00:00:16.681 --> 00:00:17.810
Nine.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.990
6' 9", that amazes me because I am

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:21.870
used to being fairly tall.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.530
I'm about a little over 6' 4".

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:26.315
If I was in the NBA I'd be a
speedy little guy, wouldn't I?

00:00:26.315 --> 00:00:27.148
(laughter)

00:00:27.148 --> 00:00:28.691
I'd be one of those little speedy guys.

00:00:28.691 --> 00:00:31.130
Exactly, and in today's game
you would be very short.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.855
Yeah, I'd be a small
untalented man in the NBA.

00:00:34.855 --> 00:00:36.510
(laughter)

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.350
My small height would
not be the only problem.

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:40.400
There'd be other problems too.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:41.460
I didn't want to say that.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:42.877
[Conan] Thank you, you're kind.

00:00:42.877 --> 00:00:43.710
I'm glad you said that.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:48.710
Thank you, but I'm curious
this causes problems for you.

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:50.900
Everyone thinks it would be
so great to be Magic Johnson,

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.040
but six feet nine inches tall,

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.990
you've actually broken equipment

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:57.455
at an amusement park, didn't you?

00:00:57.455 --> 00:00:58.288
(laughing)

00:00:58.288 --> 00:00:59.121
Tell us about that, what did you do?

00:00:59.121 --> 00:01:02.770
Oh man, what happened was
I got on a roller coaster.

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:06.290
And you know the bars that lock you in,

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:09.118
I had to fold my legs in sit like this,

00:01:09.118 --> 00:01:12.780
really down low so the bar
could come over and lock me in.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:13.613
Right.

00:01:13.613 --> 00:01:17.720
Well, it threw the timing
off the whole roller coaster.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.271
So everyone was killed?

00:01:19.271 --> 00:01:21.300
(laughter)

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.710
What a wonderful story!

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:23.543
Basically.

00:01:23.543 --> 00:01:25.219
Just because you had to
ride a roller coaster.

00:01:25.219 --> 00:01:26.052
Yes, I had to ride.

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:27.750
So it took us like 10
minutes to get me in there.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:28.583
[Conan] Right, right.

00:01:28.583 --> 00:01:30.920
And so when we finished the ride,

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:33.980
there was about eight
blue coats waiting for me.

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:36.300
And I was like, uh-oh, what happened?

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.020
I thought something had happened.

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:40.197
So they pulled me aside and said,

00:01:40.197 --> 00:01:44.147
"Mr. Johnson, you can never
ride a roller coaster again."

00:01:45.428 --> 00:01:46.540
That's so sad.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:47.750
Very sad.

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.609
So then you went to the
tea cups, and broke those.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:50.820
Just went around.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.100
Everything at the park
I should have broke,

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.410
but I had a good time, though.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:55.840
It was an experience.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.510
Now you did, I don't know who came up

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:00.670
with the nickname Magic,
but if you're gonna

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:01.947
pick a nickname, I would think

00:02:01.947 --> 00:02:03.790
that's one of the better
ones to have, you know?

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.580
Because a lot of people get
saddled with a nickname,

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.290
and then that is it.

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:08.660
So did you have someone?

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:10.020
I mean, who first of all
came up with the idea

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.460
of let's call this guy Magic.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:12.293
Was that you?

00:02:12.293 --> 00:02:13.126
No, it wasn't me.

00:02:13.126 --> 00:02:15.760
It was a sports writer
back in Lansing, Michigan

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:17.520
when I was 15 years old.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.153
And he said, hey I want
to give you a nickname.

00:02:19.153 --> 00:02:22.620
And you know at 15, what do you know?

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:23.453
Nothing really.

00:02:23.453 --> 00:02:24.650
[Conan] Right, right.

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:25.950
And so, I said okay, cool.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:27.640
And my friends are all laughing at me,

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:30.510
so the guy said, somebody's
already called Doctor J,

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:32.460
and Big E, that was Elvin Hayes.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:34.060
I want to call you Magic.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:36.610
So I looked at my boys, they looked at me.

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:38.540
Is this guy kidding?

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:39.840
And I thought he was kidding, too,

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.840
and the next day he
wrote the article Magic,

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:42.930
and it stuck ever since then.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:44.390
That's giving that guy a lot of power.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:47.273
If he had said stinky, you know?

00:02:47.273 --> 00:02:51.150
I think you're stinky,
and then that sticks,

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.290
and no matter what you achieve,

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:53.790
they're like good job, stinky.

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:57.530
You had a different nickname for a while

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:58.960
that you got rid of, isn't that right?

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.900
Yeah, oh man, a few of them.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.371
My family called me June Bug.

00:03:03.371 --> 00:03:04.610
(laughing)

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:05.790
See, that would not be nearly.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:09.260
And then June Bug won his fifth NBA title.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:10.093
Exactly.

00:03:10.093 --> 00:03:12.050
Go June Bug, go!

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:14.240
That just wouldn't be very good.

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.201
You're right, and so you know,

00:03:16.201 --> 00:03:19.050
Little E, EJ, you know.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:22.400
And then the Lakers,
they all called me Buck.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:23.233
[Conan] Right.

00:03:23.233 --> 00:03:24.700
So that was my name with the Lakers.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:25.627
Right, right.

00:03:25.627 --> 00:03:27.177
But Magic, you can't beat that.

00:03:27.177 --> 00:03:28.979
No, you can't beat it.

00:03:28.979 --> 00:03:30.530
It's great, it's been good to me.

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:33.293
My mom, she doesn't like
it, but it's been great.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:35.530
Why doesn't you're mom like it?

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:38.313
Well, you know, of course
they give you Earvin.

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:41.410
What's wrong with Earvin?

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:44.070
Let me talk to her, yeah.

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:46.400
I'll explain to her Earvin's okay, but no,

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:47.233
it's not as good as Magic.

00:03:47.233 --> 00:03:48.570
Well the funny thing is, Conan,

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:52.120
Earvin is not the reason that
she lives in that big house.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.939
I had to keep explaining,
Magic is the reason.

00:03:54.939 --> 00:03:55.980
(applause and laughter)

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:57.863
Magic paid for this.

00:03:57.863 --> 00:04:00.783
Earvin's working in a
shoe store somewhere.

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:07.070
Now you not only achieved
great things as an athlete,

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.550
an amazingly successful businessman.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.080
And I was looking at your
accomplishments today.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:16.006
You own 33 Starbucks, and
that's on one city block.

00:04:16.006 --> 00:04:18.360
(laughter)

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.910
Which is a problem, by
the way, we have enough.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:23.510
You have a chain of movie
theaters, is that right?

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:27.290
24-hour gyms, you're
part owner of the Lakers,

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:30.310
and then you own TGI
Fridays, is that right?

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:31.290
Yeah, that's it.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.130
Do you go to TGI Fridays?

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.660
Yes, I do, I enjoy it.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:36.550
[Conan] There's some good
stuff at TGI Fridays.

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:37.383
Yeah, some good stuff.

00:04:37.383 --> 00:04:39.280
And you have Fatburger restaurants.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:42.360
Yeah, it's a southern
California hamburger stand,

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:44.200
which we have 47 units.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:47.320
Right, I used to go to
Fatburger all the time,

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:48.440
and then I was wondering do they

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:49.830
ever try to get you to change it

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:51.380
to sound more healthy conscious,

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:52.560
but leave the burgers the same.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.640
You might not want to call it Fatburger.

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:56.020
Yes.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:57.503
Try the artery clogger.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:00.481
You're gonna love it.

00:05:00.481 --> 00:05:01.960
(laughter)

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.825
You got me on that one.

00:05:03.825 --> 00:05:04.658
Yeah, but you know my favorite is

00:05:04.658 --> 00:05:07.980
you are partners in a
bank with Janet Jackson.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:10.110
Yeah, we're business partners.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:11.070
See, first of all that sounds like

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:13.480
the coolest bank in the world.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:14.313
Where you going?

00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:15.600
Janet Jackson and Magic Johnson's bank.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.655
I want to come.

00:05:17.655 --> 00:05:18.488
That sounds like a cool bank.

00:05:18.488 --> 00:05:20.410
The other thing is, I think
the problem with having a bank

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:21.940
is that if someone hits you up for money

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:24.690
and you own a bank, it's very hard to say,

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.030
I don't know, it's not a
good time for me right now.

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:31.070
You own a bank, you know what I mean?

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:34.027
They can say just take me
to any one of your ATMs.

00:05:34.027 --> 00:05:35.930
And it's been hard to turn people down

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:37.143
because of that reason, you're right.

00:05:37.143 --> 00:05:39.374
Especially the relatives.

00:05:39.374 --> 00:05:41.820
You own a bank.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:42.930
I don't want to hear that you don't

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:44.240
have any money right now.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:45.900
Now, one thing that's set you apart,

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:47.260
which I think is a great thing,

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:50.100
especially when you consider the NBA today

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:53.600
is that you never cursed,
you never trash talked

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:54.980
when you were a player.

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:58.630
But people must have trash talked at you.

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:00.783
And how did you handle that?

00:06:00.783 --> 00:06:03.380
Did you just try and let it wash over you?

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:04.630
How did you tune that out?

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:05.930
When someone's right
there and they're just

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:08.100
giving you a hard time and they're saying

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.130
all kinds of nasty stuff to
try to get into your head,

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:11.160
how did you respond?

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:14.000
Well, it was funny because
they'd be running their mouth,

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.563
and I'd point up at the scoreboard,

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:19.760
because nine times out of 10,

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:21.610
we were beating that same team.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:23.400
Yeah, yeah, so that's all you had to do.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:24.785
I thought you were gonna say

00:06:24.785 --> 00:06:26.704
and then you pressed a button
and it fell on the guy.

00:06:26.704 --> 00:06:28.860
(laughter)

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:30.720
Pretty good, see that?

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:31.553
Click!

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:35.130
No, I just let the
scoreboard do the talking

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:37.000
because when you're winning,

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.530
at that time I didn't trash talk.

00:06:39.530 --> 00:06:40.820
The biggest two trash talkers

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:42.250
ever in the history of basketball

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.260
is Michael Jordan and Larry Bird.

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:46.290
But they can back it up.

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:48.370
See, that's what's so great about

00:06:48.370 --> 00:06:50.150
basketball players in my day.

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:51.940
Michael Jordan could back it up.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:53.167
He would let you know he's killing you

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:54.240
and he would kill you.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:56.500
He would score 50, and
Larry Bird would say

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:57.590
I'm gonna score 40 tonight,

00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:58.760
and go out and score 40.

00:06:58.760 --> 00:06:59.593
[Conan] Right.

00:06:59.593 --> 00:07:01.110
And win the game.

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:03.696
Now guys talk trash and they can't play.

00:07:03.696 --> 00:07:05.370
(laughter)

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:07.740
You know what, that's
exactly what I would be

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:09.260
if I was in the NBA.

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:11.350
I would be that guy,
like (angry gibberish),

00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:13.150
and then I would accomplish nothing.

00:07:14.083 --> 00:07:17.030
But I'd be trash talking
more than anybody.

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:19.000
Yes, and that's what we have more today

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.422
than we have actual
great basketball players.

00:07:21.422 --> 00:07:23.720
So we have to change that sort of speak.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:25.120
Now let's talk about Who's Got Game.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:26.070
This is an interesting idea.

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:28.444
This is your show, tell us about it.

00:07:28.444 --> 00:07:29.277
It's on MTV.

00:07:29.277 --> 00:07:30.750
It's a street ball reality show on MTV

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:32.710
starting this Sunday at 10:30.

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:36.180
And actually Snoop Dogg's
show premiers before my show.

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:39.160
And what it is, we went around the country

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:42.030
and casted different players
from around the country.

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:45.200
And these are guys that are
amazing players, but they play

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:46.907
Street ball only.

00:07:46.907 --> 00:07:47.840
Just on the street.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:49.320
They play in courts
just around the country.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:53.070
At their hometown and they
never played in the NBA

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:54.770
or any professional league.

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:56.140
And this is their shot.

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:59.370
This is their chance to be
on TV for the first time,

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:00.620
people can watch them play,

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:03.650
because street ball is
really big, like in New York.

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:06.140
It's really popular here, Chicago.

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:08.050
Crowds gather and watch these games.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:10.420
And these guys have names, too.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:13.096
They have Helicopter and this and that,

00:08:13.096 --> 00:08:16.060
White Chocolate and
they have different type

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:16.893
[Conan] White Chocolate.

00:08:16.893 --> 00:08:17.726
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:17.726 --> 00:08:19.163
I wish I had grabbed that one.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:22.684
Late Night with White Chocolate.

00:08:22.684 --> 00:08:25.451
(laughter)

00:08:25.451 --> 00:08:27.492
Hiya folks, how are ya?

00:08:27.492 --> 00:08:29.692
White Chocolate coming at you.

00:08:29.692 --> 00:08:31.057
And they're legends.

00:08:31.057 --> 00:08:34.403
And they're like Michael
Jordan in their hometown.

00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:36.960
They all compete against each other.

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:38.837
Compete against each other
for 100 thousand dollars

00:08:38.837 --> 00:08:42.830
and a court renamed and
refurbished in their hometown.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:47.190
And so there'll be one winner
after the 10th episode.

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:48.924
So it's amazing, it's really great.

00:08:48.924 --> 00:08:49.757
And you have women in there, too.

00:08:49.757 --> 00:08:51.430
Women, we have 10 guys, two women,

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:54.190
and we also tell the
backstory of them, as well.

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:56.480
We follow them around to their hometown,

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:58.490
as well as they all
live in the same place.

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:01.250
That's a part of all these reality shows.

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:03.870
Make them hate each other by
having to share a bathroom.

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:05.640
Yes, and you know what's funny?

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:08.410
In sports and in this show

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:10.920
they end up supporting the winner.

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:13.910
Really because that's
what sports is about.

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:16.740
We really respect the
person who is the best.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:18.890
Like, I don't hate Michael Jordan.

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:20.000
He was the best.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:21.900
I didn't hate Larry Bird.

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:23.630
You know, we just disliked
each other on the court

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:25.800
when we went after the championship,

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:27.910
but at the end of the
day we respect each other

00:09:27.910 --> 00:09:29.680
because he's a talented guy.

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:32.260
You have to give it up
to talented players.

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:34.980
Much different than in other arenas

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:37.340
where they dislike people.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:39.020
Right, right, or they
try and run them down

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:40.990
or say they could never take me.

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:42.660
Oh yeah, that's trash talking?

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:45.200
Yeah, that's just my whole mentality.

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:46.033
That's how I am.

00:09:46.033 --> 00:09:47.670
I'm like, what are you
talking about support the guy?

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:49.640
No, run them down!

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:51.520
You've got it all wrong, Magic.

